### 31. UNAUTHORIZED POWERED BY / CREDIT LINKS

**What to Check:**
- "Powered by" text on user-facing (frontend) pages
- Credit links displayed without explicit opt-in
- Attribution in footers, widgets, or visible plugin output
- Links back to plugin developer's website on frontend

**Problematic Patterns:**
```php
// In frontend output
<span>Powered by <a href="https://example.com">Plugin Name</a></span>
<div class="credits">Made with ❤️ by Developer</div>
<p class="plugin-credit">Built by <a href="...">Company</a></p>

// React/JSX
<span className="footer-text">Powered by <a href="https://example.com" target="_blank">Service</a></span>

// Automatic credit insertion
echo '<div class="powered-by">Powered by ' . PLUGIN_NAME . '</div>';
```

**What Is Allowed:**
- Attribution in admin-facing areas (plugin settings pages)
- Attribution in source code comments (required for GPL)
- Serviceware embeds (Twitter, YouTube, Disqus) showing their own branding
- Credit links with EXPLICIT opt-in (user must check a box to enable)

**What Is NOT Allowed:**
- Any frontend attribution without explicit user consent
- Pre-checked boxes for showing credits (must be opt-in, not opt-out)
- Credits that appear by default
- Hidden or hard-to-remove attribution

**Correct Implementation (if offering optional attribution):**
```php
// In settings - unchecked by default
<label>
    <input type="checkbox" name="show_credit" value="1" 
           <?php checked(get_option('show_credit'), 1); ?>>
    Display "Powered by" credit on my site (optional)
</label>

// Only show if explicitly enabled
if (get_option('show_credit') === '1') {
    echo '<span>Powered by Plugin</span>';
}
```

**Report Format:**
```
ISSUE: Unauthorized powered by / credit link
FILE: [path]
LINE: [number]
CODE: [the credit/attribution code]
LOCATION: [frontend/user-facing]
FIX: Remove credit from frontend, OR implement explicit opt-in checkbox (unchecked by default) in plugin settings
```

